# CONTEXT BUDGET — Budget and evaluation overhead

## Policy: {{BUDGET_POLICY}}

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Budget unit | {{BUDGET_UNIT}} |
| Work-unit budget | {{UNIT_BUDGET}} |
| At 80% | Finish the current unit, checkpoint, and start nothing new |
| At 100% | Checkpoint immediately, then end or replace the session |
| Startup read limit | HARNESS.md, spec, task/self-evaluation state, memory index, selected memory and current refs |

## Harness-effect evaluation budget

- `harness-spec.json self_evaluation.budget_ratio` caps evaluation cost relative to operating cost.
- Budget and cooldown defer optional interval or sample evaluations. They never defer mandatory full evaluation for canonical changes or parity/cold-start failures.
- On `decision=none`, do not read harness-evaluation or improvement documents.
- Account for task-evaluator cost and harness-effect evaluation cost separately.
- Enforce limits.max_instruction_lines, memory.max_document_lines, and memory.max_summary_chars; split optional detail into indexed references.

## Offloading

Write long lists and intermediate results to files, then read only the required sections. Use deterministic scripts to extract and aggregate journal data instead of loading the full journal into context.

